Own chunk size 0x21, malloc_usable_size = 24 = logical array size. The NEXT
chunk's size field is at p+24 and reads 0x21 in this matched baseline.

=== count=3 baseline already tracked in placement/evidence/plain-safe.out ===
logical=36 usable=40, nextsize=0000000000000021 at p+40.
Again the next chunk's size field begins exactly at the logical array end.

=== structural consequence ===
ExtractData copies elemSize=16 into sizeof(aiVector3D)=12 per element. The
last of count writes starts at p+12*(count-1) = logical_end-12 and ends at
logical_end+4: the overrun is always FOUR bytes, the final element's 4th
component, regardless of count. On this glibc the four bytes land on the next
chunk's size field (low half), not on a live aiMesh field or heap-object
payload. ASan has a redzone there instead (placement/evidence/asan-vuln.out).

=== chosen next-chunk-size sweep, VEC4 count=2, wbits = low 4 bytes ===
Each case keeps JSON length 509 and all bytes except the final float's bits.
